<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('partials/html-head', {title: "Privacy policy"}); -%>

<body>
  <div id="app" class="wrap">
    <%- include('partials/header', {title: "Privacy"}); -%>

    <section>

      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> <i>27 October, 2026</i></p>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information Veenew collects and how it is used.</p>

      <h3>Information We Collect</h3>
      <p>Veenew collects your email address, username and password when you create an account. Your password is stored only in a hashed form. Your email is used for authentication, account identification, and communication related to your account. We also store the content you create, such as posts, pages, bookmarks, microblogs and photos, and the browser and device name of each device you sign in from, so we can keep you logged in and sign you out when you ask.</p>

      <h3>Information From Visitors</h3>
      <p>Visitors to a blog can sign its guestbook or subscribe to it by email, without having an account. When a visitor signs a guestbook, Veenew collects the name, email address and message they enter. When a visitor subscribes, Veenew collects their email address. We use a visitor's email only to confirm their entry or subscription, and to email them the new posts they subscribed to, with a link to unsubscribe in every email.</p>
      <p>This information belongs to the blog it was entered on. The blog's owner can see the names, email addresses and messages in their guestbook and the email addresses of their subscribers, and is also emailed a confirmed guestbook entry. Only the name, message and date of guestbook entries the owner has approved are shown publicly, never the email address. Entries and subscriptions that are not confirmed are removed automatically after one day, and a subscriber's address is removed when they unsubscribe. To have a guestbook entry removed, contact the blog's owner or email <a href="mailto:vasanth@veenew.com">vasanth@veenew.com</a>.</p>

      <h3>How We Use Your Information</h3>
      <p>The information we collect is used to operate and maintain Veenew. Your email helps us authenticate your account, display your profile and posts, communicate with you if necessary, and keep the service secure. We only use your information for purposes related to running the platform.</p>

      <h3>Cookies</h3>
      <p>On the main site, Veenew uses two cookies. A session cookie stores an authentication key so the system can recognize that you are logged in. A security cookie stores a token that protects the forms and requests you send against cross-site request forgery. Both are used only for login and security. We do not use tracking or advertising cookies, and Veenew sets no cookies on individual blog subdomains or custom domains.</p>

      <h3>Scripts on Blogs</h3>
      <p>Blog owners can add their own scripts and styles to their blog. Veenew does not control or review them. A script a blog owner adds can set cookies or collect information from that blog's visitors, and the blog owner is responsible for it. Veenew itself adds no cookies and no analytics to blogs.</p>

      <h3>Analytics</h3>
      <p>Veenew uses Cabin Analytics, a privacy-first web analytics service, to understand general usage of the platform and improve the service. Cabin Analytics is designed to collect privacy-friendly, aggregated usage information and does not use advertising or behavioral tracking. Analytics is only collected on the root domain and not on user subdomains.</p>

      <h3>What We Don't Do</h3>
      <p>Veenew does not sell your personal data and does not share your information with third parties except as described in this document or when required by law. We do not use advertising technologies, behavioral profiling, or invasive tracking systems to monitor your activity.</p>

      <h3>Your Rights</h3>
      <p>You are in control of your account and content. You can edit your profile, export your data (posts, pages, bookmarks, microblogs, guestbook entries, subscribers and a list of your photos with links to download them), and delete your content and your account.</p>

      <h3>Data Retention</h3>
      <p>To delete your account, you first delete all your content: posts, pages, bookmarks, microblogs, photos, guestbook entries, subscribers and your favicon. Your account is then scheduled for deletion and permanently removed after 7 days, including your email address and other account information. If you log back in during those 7 days, the deletion is cancelled. Access logs are automatically deleted after a short retention period, typically within seven days.</p>

      <h3>Legal Requests</h3>
      <p>In certain situations, Veenew may be required to provide information such as your email address or access logs if requested by law or through a valid legal process.</p>

      <h3>Data Hosting</h3>
      <p>Veenew relies on trusted third-party infrastructure providers to host our source code and store your data in secure environments. The application is hosted on DigitalOcean App Platform, and user data is stored in MongoDB Atlas (MongoDB Cloud). These providers are responsible for maintaining the underlying infrastructure and security of the environments in which the service operates.</p>

      <h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
      <p>Veenew uses these other services to run the platform:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Amazon Web Services (SES)</strong> sends every email Veenew sends, such as account verification, password reset, guestbook and subscription confirmations, and new post emails to subscribers. It receives the recipient's email address and the content of the message.</li>
        <li><strong>Amazon Web Services (S3)</strong> stores the photos and favicons you upload.</li>
        <li><strong>PayPal</strong> is used to pay for a custom domain. PayPal handles your payment details under its own privacy policy. Veenew does not collect or store them, and only uses what PayPal shows about the payment to confirm it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Security</h3>
      <p>We take reasonable measures to protect your information and keep the platform secure, but no system can guarantee complete security.</p>

      <h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
      <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Continued use of Veenew after changes are made indicates acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>If you have questions about this policy, please email <a href="mailto:vasanth@veenew.com">vasanth@veenew.com</a>.</p>

    </section>
  </div>
  <%- include('partials/footer'); -%>
</body>

</html>